## QUICK FACTS FOR CONVERSATIONS

### DOT Drug Panel
- 5 drugs: Marijuana, Cocaine, Opioids, Amphetamines, PCP
- Initial screen → Confirmation test (GC/MS) for positives only

### Cutoffs (Most Common)
| Drug | Screen | Confirm |
|---|---|---|
| THC | 50 ng/mL | 15 ng/mL |
| Cocaine | 150 ng/mL | 100 ng/mL |
| Amphetamines | 500 ng/mL | 250 ng/mL |

### Post-Accident Testing
- Fatality = ALWAYS test
- Citation + injury or tow = test required
- No citation = no test required
- Alcohol: within 8 hours (2 hours preferred)
- Drug: within 32 hours (ASAP)

### Random Testing Rates
- FMCSA (trucking): 50% drug, 10% alcohol
- FTA (transit): 50% drug, 10% alcohol

### FMCSA Clearinghouse — Identity Verification (Jun 2026)
- **Existing C/TPA accounts** (DDI) must complete identity verification by **July 6, 2026**
- Path: Log in → **My Dashboard → My Profile** → **Begin Identity Verification**
- After deadline: no Clearinghouse access until completed
- Full detail: `COMPLIANCE_KNOWLEDGE/CLEARINGHOUSE_IDENTITY_VERIFICATION.md`

### Fatal Flaws (Test Cancelled)
- No collector signature
- No donor signature (uncorrected)
- Specimen ID mismatch
- Broken seal
- Insufficient volume
- No printed collector name (unidentifiable)

### Refusal = Positive
- Fails to appear
- Leaves before complete
- Refuses observation (when required)
- Shy bladder with no medical explanation
- Admits adulteration

